, it served as a significant cultural and political hub under various dynasties, including the Mauryas, Kushans, and later the Muslim rulers of Kashmir. Its strategic location along trade routes connecting Central Asia and the Indian subcontinent further accentuates its historical importance, making it a melting pot of diverse cultures and influences.

